_3D.ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
Sets which part of the object designated by <Path> is an obstacle for the Worker when he is walking freely
within the area of the model.
Remarks
To show the Barred Areas/Obstacles for the Worker in your model, press the o key on your keyboard or
click 
  on the tab View of the Frame window.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.ObstacleForWorker:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify one of the following settings:
Setting Description Looks like this
"Bounding box" The bounding box of the entire object is an Obstacle
for the Worker around which he has to walk. This
applies for example for the material flow objects, such
as the Station, etc., and for graphics.
For the Workplace Plant Simulation shows two
bounding boxes with a gap in between. This ensures
that the Worker only stays on the middle of the
Workplace. The Worker first has to leave the Workplace
before he can change his walking direction forward the
next destination object.
Bounding box is the most performant setting.
_3D.ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-951
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Setting Description Looks like this
"Bounding box of
visible graphics"
The bounding box of the entire object is an Obstacle
for the Worker around which he has to walk. Graphic
groups, which are hidden at the moment, are not
considered.
Length-oriented objects and Frames do not provide this
setting.
"Graphics" The individual graphics of the object are an Obstacle
for the Worker around which he has to walk.
In the example to the right the Worker can walk
through the pillars and the Station without having to
walk around the overall obstacle.
This applies for example for the length-oriented
material flow objects, such as the Conveyor.
For the object Conveyor Plant Simulation approximates
the display of the bounding box only roughly to the
curve, i.e., it does not show the curve of the conveyor
as a smooth curved line.
The setting Graphics can have negative effects on the
performance when you switch the display often.
_3D.ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
12-952 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Setting Description Looks like this
"Visible graphics" The graphics of the object are an Obstacle for
the Worker around which he has to walk. Graphic
groups, which are hidden at the moment, are not
considered. This applies for example for the length-
oriented material flow objects, such as the Conveyor.
The setting Visible graphics can have negative effects
on the performance when you switch the display often.
"(None)" The object is no obstacle for the Worker. He can walk
through the object or across it. This applies for example
for the information flow objects, such as the Method,
etc.
Examples
Station._3D.ObstacleForWorker := "Graphics"
PickAndPlace._3D.ObstacleForWorker := "(None)"
SimTalk
_3D.getGraphic.ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk] of a graphic
