createExtrusionGraphic [SimTalk]
Creates a graphic that extrudes a two-dimensional profile along a three-dimensional vector in the graphic
or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
You can create the profiles using the F3DGenerate... functions or use fully user-defined profiles.
A profile needs to surround an area and is not allowed to intersect itself.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createExtrusionGraphic(Profile:length[2,*], 
ExtrusionVector:length[3], ClosedShape:boolean) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Profile is a two-dimensional array of data type length with two values. They designate
the profile that will be extruded.
• The parameter ExtrusionVector is an array of data type length with three values. They designate the
vector along which the profile will be extruded.
• The parameter ClosedShape of data type boolean specifies whether the created graphic shall be a closed
shape in which case it will have a cover face at the start and at the end, or a hollow shape in which case
you can look through the graphic when you look along the extrusion vector.
Note
You can create closed shapes with holes. In such a case, the shape is closed but the profile surrounds a
hole, compare the examples below.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created graphic, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
createExtrusionGraphic [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-967
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Examples
-- This creates a closed but hollow extruded ellipse: You can see through 
the hole but not through the graphic.
MyObject._3D.getGraphic("default").createExtrusionGraphic(F3DgenerateHollowE
llipse([0m, 0m], 2m, 3m, 0.1m, 0.1m), [2m, 0m, 0m], true)
-- This creates a closed cylinder: You cannot see through anything.
MyObject._3D.getGraphic("default").createExtrusionGraphic(F3DgenerateEllips
e([5m, 0m], 2m, 2m, 0.1m, 0.1m), [0m, 2m, 0m], true)
-- This creates the shell of a cylinder: You cannot see through anything.
MyObject._3D.getGraphic("default").createExtrusionGraphic(F3DgenerateEllips
e([-5m, 0m], 2m, 2m, 0.1m, 0.1m), [0m, 0m, 2m], false)
See also
_Detailed Access To Graphics
