createFence [SimTalk]
Creates a fence in the graphic or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Initially the created graphic does not have any materials. You can set these later.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createFence(Dimensions:length[3], Mesh:boolean, Panes:boolean[, 
FenceElementWidth:length]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Dimensions is an array of data type length with three values.
They designate the Dimension X, the Dimension Y, and the Dimension Z of the fence.
• The parameter Mesh of data type boolean sets if a wire mesh is inserted between the posts of the fence
(true) or not (false).
• The parameter Panes of data type boolean sets if transparent or non-transparent panes are inserted
between the posts of the fence (true) or not (false).
• The optional parameter FenceElementWidth of data type length sets the width of the individual
elements of the fence.
Note
When you change the setting for Placing The Remainder, Plant Simulation resets the Cutouts.
