createMezzanine [SimTalk]
Creates a mezzanine in the graphic or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Initially the created graphic does not have any materials. You can set these later.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createMezzanine(Dimensions:length[3], FloorThickness:length, 
PostDiameter:length, BorderLine:boolean, RailingSegmentWidth:length]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Dimensions is an array of data type length with three values.
They designate the Width/Dimension X, the Depth/Dimension Y, and the Height/Dimension Z of the
mezzanine.
• The parameter FloorThickness of data type length sets the floor thickness on which the platform of the
mezzanine rests.
• The parameter PostDiameter of data type length sets the diameter of the posts on which the platform of
the mezzanine rests.
• The parameter BorderLine of data type boolean sets if a borderline will be inserted around the platform
of the mezzanine (true) or not (false).
• The parameter RailingSegmentWidth of data type length sets width of the individual segments of the
railing.
The segment width is the distance between the individual posts that hold the railing. Type in 0 to
deactivate the railing. Type in a value greater than 0 to activate the railing and to set the segment width.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created graphic, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
createMezzanine [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-979
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
var mezzanine := _3D.getGraphic("deco").createMezzanine([1.5, 3.0, 2.8], 
0.08, 0.15, true, 1.0)
mezzanine.MaterialActive := true
mezzanine.MaterialDiffuseColor := makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
