createPolyLine [SimTalk]
Creates a polyline with the specified parameters in your 3D simulation model specified by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createPolyLine(Nodes:length[3,*], Diameter:length [, 
Directed:boolean:=false]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Nodes is an array of data type length.
They designate the anchor points of the polyline.
• The parameter Diameter of data type length designates the diameter of the polyline.
• The optional parameter Directed of data type boolean sets if the direction of the polyline will be shown
(true) or not (false).
Default Value of the Parameter
The default values is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created polyline, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
Example
 // The following code creates a directed polyline with 4 points, a 
diameter of 0.1 and a color of orange.
var Points = make2DimArray(3, [ 6.0, -2.0, 1.0,
                                9.0, -2.0, 1.0,
                               12.0, -4.0, 2.0,
                               15.0, -4.0, 2.0])
var PolyLine := _3D.getGraphic("deco").createPolyLine(Points, 0.1, true)
PolyLine.MaterialDiffuseColor :=  makeRGBValue(255, 128, 0)
createPolyLine [SimTalk]
