createRack [SimTalk]
Creates a rack in the graphic or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Initially the created graphic does not have any materials. You can set these later.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createRack(BaySize:length[2], BoardDepth:length, 
Capacity:integer[2], MinimalStructure:boolean[, SquarePosts:boolean:=false, 
PostDiameter:length:=40mm, BoardThickness:length:=30mm, 
GroundClearance:length]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter BaySize is an array of data type length with two values.
They designate the Width/Dimension X and the Height/Dimension Z of the individual bays of the rack.
• The parameter BoardDepth of data type length sets the depth/Dimension Y of the boards of the rack.
• The parameter Capacity is an array of data type integer with two values.
They designate the capacity of the rack, i. e., the Number of Bays per Board and the Number of
Boards.
• The parameter MinimalStructure of data type boolean sets if the optimization is aiming for
Performance (true) or for Post-processing Capability (false).
• The optional parameter SquarePosts of data type boolean sets if the rack will be created with square
posts (true) or with round posts (false). If you do not specify the parameter, the rack will be created
with round posts.
• The optional parameter PostDiameter of data type length sets the diameter of the posts of the rack.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 4 cm.
• The optional parameter BoardThickness of data type length sets the thickness of a board of the rack.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 3 cm.
createRack [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-985
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The optional parameter GroundClearance of data type length sets the distance between the lower edge
of the lowest board and the floor on which the rack sits. Type in 0 so that the rack sits flat on the floor.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created graphic, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
Example
var Rack := _3D.getGraphic("deco").createRack([1.5, 1.5], 1, [3, 4], true, 
true, 0.1, 0.05, 0.5))
Rack.MaterialActive := true
Rack.MaterialDiffuseColor := makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
See also
Rack
_Accessing Attributes of Graphic Shapes > _Rack Attributes
_Detailed Access To Graphics
