createStairs [SimTalk]
Creates a staircase in the graphic or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Initially the created graphic does not have any materials. You can set these later.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createStairs(TreadWidth:length, Rise:length, 
StartAtFirstTread:boolean) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter TreadWidth of data type length sets the tread width. This is the width of the steps and
thus the width of the entire stairway.
• The parameter Rise of data type length sets the rise. This is the height of the entire stairway from the
floor of one floor to the ceiling of the next floor.
• The parameter StartAtFirstTread of data type length sets if the staircase starts at the first tread without
the stringer jutting out onto the floor on which the stairway rests (true) or not (false).
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created graphic, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
Example
var Stairs := _3D.getGraphic("deco").createStairs(1.5, 3, true)
Stairs.MaterialActive := true
Stairs.MaterialDiffuseColor := makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
See also
Stairs
createStairs [SimTalk]
12-990 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

