createTiledPlate [SimTalk]
Creates a plate which shows the picture or the texture loaded from a picture tiled in the graphic or graphic
group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
If your model contains several partially or fully transparent graphics behind each other from your current
view point, it can happen that some or all of these graphics look wrong or seem to be missing.
This is due to heuristics without which the rendering performance would drastically decrease.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createTiledPlate(FilePath:string, Orientation:integer, 
Size:length[2], Bifacial:boolean, TileSize:length[2][, 
Thickness:length:=1mm, UseTransparency:boolean:=true]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets the path and the name of the file you want to import.
• The parameter Orientation of data type integer sets the sets the orientation of the picture.
1 stands for Floor, 2 stands for Front Wall, and 3 stands for Side Wall.
• The parameter Size is an array of data type length with two values.
They designate the Width and the Height of the picture. If you enter a value less than or equal to 0 for
one of the values for one of the two values, the respective other value is calculated from the width to
height ratio. You can enter a maximum Width or Height of 32767 pixels.
• The parameter Bifacial of data type boolean sets if the texture will be shown on both sides of the plate
(true) or only on the top side of the plate (false).
• The parameter TileSize is an array of data type length with two values.
They designate the Width/Tile Size X and the Depth/Tile Size Y of a tile. If you enter a value less than or
equal to 0 for one of the values for one of the two values, the respective other value is calculated from
the width to height ratio.
• The optional parameter Thickness of data type length designates the thickness of the plate.
Default Value of the Parameter
createTiledPlate [SimTalk]
12-994 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The default value is 1 mm.
• The optional parameter UseTransparency of data type boolean sets if transparent or partially
transparent pixels in the texture are shown transparent (true) or if Plant Simulation enforces opacity
(false). If you don't specify this parameter, Plant Simulation will use transparency.
If the image file does not contain transparent pixels, the parameter has no effect.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is true.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It designates the created graphic, compare the method _3D.getGraphic.
Example
var TiledPlate := _3D.getGraphic("deco").createTiledPlate("D:\Picture.png", 
1, [4.0,2.0], true, [2.0, 2.0], 0.1)
TiledPlate.MaterialActive := true
TiledPlate.MaterialDiffuseColor := makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
See also
Textured Plate
