importGraphics [SimTalk]
Imports the specified graphic from the file and adds it to the existing graphic in the graphic or graphic
group designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation can import files of these types:
Note
Plant Simulation uses the file name of the graphic as the name of the graphic node.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.importGraphics(FilePath:string[, YUpToZUp:boolean:=false, 
MoveContentToZero:boolean:=false]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets path to the graphic to be imported.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
• The optional parameter YUpToZUp of data type boolean sets if up-direction, i. e., the y-direction of the
imported graphic, will be converted from the y-direction to the z-direction (true) or not (false).
• The optional parameter MoveContentToZero of data type boolean sets if the visible center of the
imported graphic is to be moved to the center of the scene defined by the coordinates 0,0,0 (true) or
not (false).
importGraphics [SimTalk]
12-996 Plant Simulation Help
